# Each non-empty line is a list item in the compatibility disclosure.
compose-compatibility-note = The most widely supported post type across the fediverse. Expect it to look much as it does here on the vast majority of servers.

compose-compatibility-article = Mastodon shows the title and a link to Plamenu, with no article body. Readers must open that link to read the article; they can still reply and boost on Mastodon. *oma, *key, GoToSocial and Mitra receive and show the full article text and title, so readers can read it in their client.

compose-compatibility-event = Mastodon shows the event name and a link to Plamenu. The description, dates, venue and RSVP controls are absent from its timeline post. Mobilizon can display the event and lets its users RSVP from their own accounts, but expect some turbulence as we work out the compatibility details. Likes and boosts do not register attendance.

compose-compatibility-group = Lemmy displays a titled group post as a community discussion with its title, body, and first attachment. Replies appear as comments in that discussion. Mastodon shows the title and a link to Plamenu, with no discussion body. Its users can reply from Mastodon; reading the full post requires opening the link.
